  ],
  "cultivar_name": "Anthurium 'Dark Mama'",
  "formula_status": "disputed",
  "id": 5,
  "name_status": "disputed",
  "origins": [
   {
    "author": {
     "date": "2026-10-03",
     "isAI": true,
     "name": "AI 要約（2026-10-03、引用元の本文と照合）"
    },
    "body": "John Banta が作出し \"Dark Moma\" と名付けた Anthurium warocqueanum の交配種に始まる名前。Jay Vannini は 2003 年に同じ交配（A. warocqueanum × A. papillilaminum 'Fort Sherman'、正逆とも）を作り直し、2006 年に NSE Tropicals へ実生を送った。綴りは Dark Momma なども使われたが、流通で定着したのは NSE Tropicals が広めた 'Dark Mama'。Vannini はこの 2 種の単純交配はすべて Dark Mama になると書いている（ただし流通する papillilaminum には交配株が多い）。",
    "body_en": "The name goes back to John Banta's Anthurium warocqueanum hybrid, which he christened \"Dark Moma\". Jay Vannini remade the cross in 2003 (A. warocqueanum × A. papillilaminum 'Fort Sherman', both ways) and sent seedlings to NSE Tropicals in 2006. Spellings such as Dark Momma circulated, but 'Dark Mama', popularised by NSE Tropicals, prevailed in the trade. Vannini writes that all simple crosses of these two species produce Dark Mama (many papillilaminum in cultivation are bench hybrids).",
    "source_name": "Exotica Esoterica (Jay Vannini)",
    "source_tier": "B",
    "source_type": "ai_research",
    "source_url": "https://www.exoticaesoterica.com/magazine/the-ultimate-guide-to-velvet-leaf-anthuriums",
    "sources": [
     {
      "label": "Exotica Esoterica — The ultimate guide to velvet-leaf anthuriums (Jay Vannini)",
